# Two earlier findings, rechecked at this repin:
#  - The adapter's README example (`main!` with `Try({}, _)` ending in
#    `Stdout.line!`) compiles under nightly-2026-11-01-48d3369 and
#    nightly-2026-11-03-34bd006, but not under nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27, where
#    the adapter's closed `WsClient.Error` clashes with the platform's
#    `[Exit(I32), Interrupted]`. ws_client keeps the adapter's own pattern
#    (a function returning `WsClient.Error`, `main!` mapping it to `Exit(1)`),
#    which compiles under all three.
#  - Under nightly-2026-11-01-48d3369 a program on basic-cli 0.26.0 that calls
#    Tcp `read_up_to!` twice on one connection aborts at run time ("is not a
#    live TcpConnection handle: it has already been freed"). It runs under
#    nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27 and under nightly-2026-11-03-34bd006, so the
#    fault is gone with the newer nightly. The client and server topics ran
#    against each other under both of those.

